-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/0251f3b5-0c31-5a58-a394-58280de94f02
-- title:
--   A uniform transfer constant in the hyperbolic-term base-change comparison
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension, and $\sigma : L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ is an automorphism such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`hgen`), the degree $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ being prime (`hdeg`). Write $\mathbb{A}_F$ for the adele ring of a number field $F$ and $\mathrm{AdelicGL2}$ for $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$; `globalPoints` is the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(F) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ induced by $F \to \mathbb{A}_F$, `centralScalar` sends an idele $z$ to the scalar matrix $z \cdot 1$, and $\mathrm{ideleNorm}$ is the module of the multiplication action on $\mathbb{A}_F$.
--
--   *Truncation window and fundamental domains.* Real numbers $\alpha < \beta$ with $0 < \alpha$ are fixed. The set $\Phi_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ lies in the determinant slab $\{g : \mathrm{ideleNorm}_L(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΦs`) and is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ acting on the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` restricted to that slab (`hΦ`); $\Phi_K$ satisfies the corresponding two conditions over $K$ (`hΦKs`, `hΦK`). On the idele units, $\nu_{Z,L}$ is a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\Omega_L$ a fundamental domain for the image of $L^\times$ (`hΩL`); likewise $\nu_{Z,K}$, $\Omega_K$ over $K$ (`hΩK`).
--
--   *Descent and place data.* $D$ is an idelic Galois descent for $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $K$, i.e. an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ by continuous ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with the action on $L$; `sigmaAdelicAct` applies $D$ at $\sigma^{-1}$ entrywise to a matrix. Finite sets $S_K$ of finite places of $K$ and $S_L$ of finite places of $L$ satisfy: every place of $L$ above $S_K$ lies in $S_L$ (`hSL`); membership in $S_L$ depends only on the place of $K$ below (`hSsat`); and every place of $L$ whose place below is outside $S_K$ has ramification index $1$ (`hS`).
--
--   *Characters and levels.* $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous (`hξc`), trivial on the principal ideles (`hξt`), and takes the same value on $\det(\mathrm{heckeGen}_w)$ and $\det(\mathrm{heckeGen}_{w'})$ whenever $w, w' \notin S_L$ lie over the same place of $K$ (`hξσ`). An ideal $N \subseteq \mathcal{O}_L$ has all its prime divisors in $S_L$ (`hN`) and an ideal $N' \subseteq \mathcal{O}_K$ has all its prime divisors in $S_K$ (`hN'`). Archimedean type families $\mathrm{tys}_L$, $\mathrm{tys}_K$ are given, together with test-function components $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$, semi-local components $\varphi_S$, an archimedean component $f_{a,K}$ and local components $f_{S,K}$ over $K$.
--
--   *Hecke-eigenvalue compactum.* A compact set $X$ of functions from finite places of $L$ to $\mathbb{C} \times \mathbb{C}$ (`hXc`) is assumed (`hX`) to contain all $x$ which vanish on $S_L$ and satisfy, for $w \notin S_L$: $(x\,w)_2 = \mathrm{absNorm}(w) \cdot \xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_w)$, $\lVert (x\,w)_1 \rVert \le (\mathrm{absNorm}(w)+1)\sqrt{\lVert \xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_w)\rVert}$, and $\overline{(x\,w)_1} = \overline{(x\,w)_2}\,\lVert (x\,w)_2 \rVert^{-1} (x\,w)_1$.
--
--   *The character set downstairs.* $\Xi$ is a finite set of homomorphisms from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, characterised by `hΞ`: $\xi \in \Xi$ if and only if $\xi$ is continuous, trivial on the principal ideles of $K$, and satisfies $\xi \circ \mathrm{idelicNorm}(\mathrm{genuineBaseChange}\,K\,L) = \xi_L$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$.
--
--   *The geometric input.* A complex number $c_0$ is given together with the hypothesis `hgeo`: for every finite set $S'$ of places of $K$ containing $S_K$, every continuous compactly supported $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ which is unit-factorisable above $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ for the level $\mathrm{levelOne}(N) \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch}_L)$, and every continuous compactly supported $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ which is unit-factorisable at $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$ for $\mathrm{principalLevel}(N') \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch}_K)$, such that $\varphi$ and $f$ match at $S'$ with respect to $\sigma^{-1}$ and such that at each $v \notin S'$ all of whose places above are unramified the indicators of the semi-local and local integral sets match locally, one has
--   $$\int_{\Phi_L}\!\int_{\Omega_L} \xi_L(z) \sum_{\delta}^{\flat} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(z x)\bigr) = c_0 \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{\Phi_K}\!\int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\bigl(\mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{cen}}_f + \mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{ell}}_f\bigr)(x, z x),$$
--   where the finite sum on the left runs over those $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted norm class (via `normClassMap`) is the conjugacy class of some $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ of elliptic or central type, and $\mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{cen}}_f$, $\mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{ell}}_f$ are the finite sums of $f(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ over the central and elliptic cells of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ with $\lambda \ne 0$ such that the following two assertions hold.
--
--   (i) *Normalisation.* If there exist a finite set $S' \supseteq S_K$ of places of $K$ and functions $\varphi$, $f$ with all the regularity, factorisation, matching and unit-matching properties listed in `hgeo` and such that $\sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{\Phi_K}\int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\bigl(\mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{cen}}_f + \mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{ell}}_f\bigr)(x, zx) \ne 0$, then $[L:K]\,\lambda = c_0$.
--
--   (ii) *Hyperbolic-term comparison at every Hecke place set.* For every finite set $T$ of places of $K$ disjoint from $S_K$ with $\#T \ge 2$, all of whose places above lie outside $S_L$; for every choice of extensions $w_v \mid v$ (a family `ws` of elements of $v.\mathrm{Extension}(\mathcal{O}_L)$) and every family $w'$ of places of $L$ with $(w'_v)$ equal to the $\sigma^{-1}$-translate of the ideal of $w_v$ for $v \in T$; for every family of elements $\varpi_v$ of the valuation ring at $w_v$ which are irreducible on $T$ and have nonzero image in the completion, every $n_v$ and every family $r_{T,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ forming a Hecke coset system for the double coset of $\mathrm{diagPi}(\varpi_v)$ relative to the integral subgroup, and every family $z_v$ whose matrix is $\varpi_v \cdot 1$ on $T$; and for the corresponding data $\varpi_{K,v}$, $n_{K,v}$, $r_{K,v}$, $z_{K,v}$ over $K$ (irreducibility, nonvanishing, Hecke coset system for $\mathrm{diagPi}(\varpi_{K,v})$ relative to the integral subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, and scalar shape $\varpi_{K,v}\cdot 1$ on $T$): there exist natural numbers $r$, $c$, a function $s$ on the places of $K$ and two winding data $\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B}$ of shape $(r, \#T, c)$ such that
--
--   — $s_v^2 = \xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_{w'_v})$ for every $v \in T$, and
--
--   — for all families of exponents $k$, $j$ on the places of $K$, every continuous compactly supported $\varphi_L$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles of $L$ such that $\varphi_L$ admits the semi-local factorisation at $S_K \cup T$ with archimedean factor $\varphi_a$, finite factor $\varphi_f$ and semi-local factors equal, at $v \in T$, to $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota} \mathbf{1}_{\mathrm{semiLocalIntegralSet}}\bigl((\mathrm{semiLocalComponent}\,(\mathrm{localEmbed}\,(\prod_m r_{T,v}(\iota_m))\,z_v^{j_v}))^{-1} x\bigr)$, the sum being over $\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)$, and to $\varphi_S(v)$ otherwise, and such that $\varphi_L$ is bi-invariant under $\mathrm{levelOne}(N) \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch}_L)$ and archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$; and for every family `fam` indexed by the slot multi-indices $m \in \mathrm{slotIndex}(w_\bullet, k, j, T)$ (the pi-set of supports of the slot words) such that each $\mathrm{fam}(m)$ is bi-invariant under $\mathrm{principalLevel}(N') \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch}_K)$ and archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$, with $f_{a,K}$ an archimedean test factor, $f_{S,K}(v)$ a local test function for $v \in S_K$, and with a finite test factor $f\!f$ whose value at $h$, when all components outside $S_K \cup T$ are integral, is the product over $v \in S_K \cup T$ of the factor $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(m_v(0)) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_{K,v})} \mathbf{1}_{\mathrm{localIntegralSet}}\bigl(((\prod_m r_{K,v}(\iota_m))\,z_{K,v}^{m_v(1)})^{-1}x\bigr)$ for $v \in T$ and of $f_{S,K}(v)$ otherwise, which vanishes at $h$ as soon as some component outside $S_K \cup T$ is non-integral, and with $\mathrm{fam}(m)(g) = f_{a,K}(\mathrm{glArch}\,g)\, f\!f(\mathrm{glFin}\,g)$; and such that $\varphi_L$ matches at $S_K \cup T$, with respect to $\sigma^{-1}$, with $x \mapsto \sum_m \mathrm{slotFamilyCoeff}(w_\bullet,k,j,T,m)\,\mathrm{fam}(m)(x)$ —
--
--   there exists $R_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ such that for every $R \ge R_0$ the following hold. Let $\Theta_L(x,z)$ denote the twisted hyperbolic fold $\sum^{\flat}_{\delta} \varphi_L(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(zx))$, over those $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted norm class is the conjugacy class of some hyperbolic $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, minus the indicator of the set where the adelic height of $L$ exceeds $e^{R}$ times the constant term — taken along the unipotent $t \mapsto u(t)$ with respect to the measure attached by `productionPinsOf` to $L$, $\Phi_L$, the levels $\mathrm{levelOne}(\cdot) \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch}_L)$, the Hecke generators and the adelic box of $L$ (the conditioning of additive adelic Haar on that box) — of $y \mapsto \sum^{\flat}_{\delta} \varphi_L(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(y))$ over $\{\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) : \gamma_{10} = 0,\ N_{L/K}(\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}) \ne 1\}$, the whole expression being evaluated at $z\,x$. Let $\Theta_K^{m}(x,z)$ denote the analogous expression over $K$: the hyperbolic part $\mathcal{K}^{\mathrm{hyp}}_{\mathrm{fam}(m)}(x, zx)$ minus the indicator of the set where the adelic height of $K$ exceeds $e^R$ times the constant term, for the measure attached by `productionPinsOf` to $K$, $\Phi_K$, $\mathrm{principalLevel}(\cdot)\sqcap\ker(\mathrm{glArch}_K)$, the Hecke generators and the adelic box of $K$, of $y \mapsto \sum^{\flat}_{\gamma} \mathrm{fam}(m)(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ over $\{\gamma : \gamma_{10}=0,\ \gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11} \ne 1\}$. Then:
--
--   (a) for every $x$, the function $z \mapsto \xi_L(z)\,\Theta_L(x,z)$ is integrable on $\Omega_L$ for $\nu_{Z,L}$;
--
--   (b) the function $x \mapsto \int_{\Omega_L} \xi_L(z)\,\Theta_L(x,z)\,d\nu_{Z,L}$ is integrable on the canonical truncation domain of $L$ attached to $\alpha, \beta$ for `adelicGLHaar`;
--
--   (c) for every $\xi_K \in \Xi$ and every slot index $m$, the function $z \mapsto \xi_K(z)\,\Theta_K^m(x,z)$ is integrable on $\Omega_K$ for every $x$, and $x \mapsto \int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\,\Theta_K^m(x,z)\,d\nu_{Z,K}$ is integrable on the canonical truncation domain of $K$ attached to $\alpha, \beta$;
--
--   (d) the identity
--   $$\int_{\mathcal{F}_L}\!\int_{\Omega_L} \xi_L(z)\,\Theta_L(x,z) - [L:K]\,\lambda \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \sum_{m} \mathrm{slotFamilyCoeff}(m) \int_{\mathcal{F}_K}\!\int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\,\Theta_K^m(x,z) = R\,\Sigma(\mathcal{A}) + \Sigma(\mathcal{B})$$
--   holds, where $\mathcal{F}_L$, $\mathcal{F}_K$ are the canonical truncation domains of $L$ and $K$ for $\alpha, \beta$, and where for a winding datum $\mathcal{D}$ of shape $(r,\#T,c)$
--   $$\Sigma(\mathcal{D}) = \sum_{n} \Bigl(\prod_{i : \mathrm{Fin}(\#T)} \bigl(\sqrt{\mathrm{absNorm}(w'_{v_i})}\; s_{v_i}\bigr)^{k_{v_i}}\, \xi_L\bigl(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_{w'_{v_i}}\bigr)^{j_{v_i}}\, \bigl[(T + T^{-1})^{k_{v_i}}\bigr]_{n_i}\Bigr)\, \mathcal{D}.\mathrm{coeff}(n),$$
--   the outer sum running over integer vectors $n$ with $n_i \in [-k_{v_i}, k_{v_i}]$, $v_i$ denoting the $i$-th element of $T$ under `T.equivFin`, $[\cdot]_{n_i}$ the $n_i$-th coefficient of the indicated Laurent polynomial over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\mathcal{D}.\mathrm{coeff}(n) = \sum_i' \mathcal{D}.\mathrm{lam}(i)\,\mathcal{D}.\mathrm{fibreCoeff}(i)(n)$.
--
--   The force of the statement is that the single constant $\lambda$ is chosen before $T$ and before all the word, coset and uniformiser data, and that $c_0$ is identified with $[L:K]\lambda$ only under the non-vanishing hypothesis in (i).
--
--   This is the hyperbolic-term half of the comparison of twisted and untwisted trace formulae used in base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ along a cyclic extension of prime degree: after truncation at height $e^R$, the difference of the twisted hyperbolic contribution over $L$ and $[L:K]\lambda$ times the matched combination of hyperbolic contributions over $K$ is an affine function of the truncation parameter $R$ whose slope and intercept are read off from two winding data, while the elliptic and central terms already compared in `hgeo` fix the constant. Hoisting the transfer constant $\lambda$ outside the quantifier over the Hecke place set $T$ is what allows the subsequent extraction of Hecke eigenvalue identities along a sequence of place sets without reusing the non-vanishing hypothesis; the result feeds the uniform version of this comparison.
